NOTE: The measured outputs are COMBINED (C·x + α·A·(B·x))
With α=0.01, the LoRA contribution is scaled by 0.01x

To estimate C vs A·B contribution:
  - C output scale ~ pretrained weight norms (typically O(1))
  - A·B output scale ~ α × rank_scale ~ 0.01 × O(1)
  - Ratio: C / (α·A·B) ~ 1 / 0.01 = 100x

So with α=0.01, C output is ~100x larger than LoRA contribution.
